{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"content_hash":"2861af9a73966356710244eddb70a4f66935eca474db9f6aff03cfaf8fe6acc5","digest":{"component_or_area":"opcert service app worker lifecycle","key_entities":["src/rebar/opcert_service/app.py","tests/unit/test_opcert_service_app.py","asyncio.wait_for","asyncio.timeout","asyncio.to_thread","_worker","lifespan","queue.get","test_matching_guard_is_accepted","test_worker_cancellation_survives_job_completion_race","TestClient"],"problem_keywords":["python 3.11","asyncio cancellation","xdist worker crash","hang","wait_for race","cpython 86296","lifespan teardown"],"propositions":["Python 3.11 asyncio.wait_for consumes external cancellation when child future completes in the same turn, causing worker to loop with cancelling()>0 while lifespan awaits indefinitely","TestClient teardown hangs after test_matching_guard_is_accepted because the opcert worker does not promptly terminate when shutdown cancellation collides with job completion","Replacing asyncio.wait_for with asyncio.timeout semantics (Python 3.12 style) preserves external cancellation and prevents the race condition","The fix in app.py:76-83 using async with asyncio.timeout(...) around asyncio.to_thread maintains per-job timeout, 202 ACK, queue semantics, and Python 3.12+ behavior while restoring prompt cancellation termination on Python 3.11"]},"digest_hash_version":1,"model":"bedrock:us.anthropic.claude-opus-4-8","schema":"ticket_digest_v1"},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"TICKET_DIGEST","timestamp":1787422441175254001,"uuid":"c1c51497-c5be-4296-8270-3582e46b4305"}